        "# Conclusion \n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.card .conclusion-card}\n",
        "\n",
        "## Key Findings\n",
        "\n",
        "**1. HIV burden varies substantially.**  \n",
        "HIV prevalence differs considerably between countries, with the highest levels concentrated in Southern and Eastern Africa.\n",
        "\n",
        "**2. Health expenditure differs widely.**  \n",
        "Current health expenditure per capita varies substantially across countries, reflecting differences in economic resources and health-system investment.\n",
        "\n",
        "**3. The relationship is complex.**  \n",
        "The analysis does not support a simple conclusion that higher health expenditure automatically results in lower HIV prevalence. Countries with high HIV prevalence may also have high expenditure because substantial resources are needed for prevention, testing, treatment, and ARV therapy.\n",
        "\n",
        "**4. Sustained investment remains important.**  \n",
        "Continued investment in health systems, HIV prevention, testing, treatment, ARV therapy, and health-system capacity remains important for improving long-term health outcomes.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Limitations\n",
        "\n",
        "This is an observational, country-level analysis. The observed relationships should therefore be interpreted as associations rather than causal effects. Differences in epidemic history, socioeconomic conditions, healthcare access, prevention programmes, treatment coverage, and data quality may influence the results.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.card .final-message}\n",
        "### Final Message\n",
        "\n",
        "**Overall, the dashboard demonstrates how publicly available health data can be combined with Python to identify patterns in HIV prevalence, health expenditure, and health-system investment. The findings highlight the importance of sustained HIV prevention, treatment, ARV therapy, and broader health-system strengthening.**\n",
